{
  "slug": "verbos-preposicion",
  "number": 26,
  "part": 6,
  "level": "B1",
  "title": "Verbs and prepositions",
  "tagline": "Listen to, wait for, think about… and décider de.",
  "goal": "Drop the prepositions English adds, use the right preposition with verbs that differ from English, and know which verbs take de or à before an infinitive.",
  "minutes": 11,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "a-personal",
      "title": "No preposition in French",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Many English verbs need a little word after them (listen **to**, look **at**, wait **for**). Their French equivalents take the object **directly**."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["English", "French"],
          "rows": [
            ["listen **to** music", "*écouter la musique*"],
            ["look **at** the photos", "*regarder les photos*"],
            ["wait **for** the bus", "*attendre le bus*"],
            ["look **for** my keys", "*chercher mes clés*"],
            ["pay **for** the coffee", "*payer le café*"],
            ["ask **for** the bill", "*demander l'addition*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "And the other way round",
          "text": "Some verbs take *à* in French but nothing in English: *téléphoner {à} Paul* (phone Paul), *répondre {à} Marie* (answer Marie), *obéir {à} ses parents*, *ressembler {à} son père* (look like). And *parler {à}* (talk to) [[15]]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "otra-preposicion",
      "title": "Verbs with a different preposition",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "These verbs take a different preposition from English. Learn them as a block, verb + preposition."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["English", "French", "Example"],
          "rows": [
            ["think **about**", "*penser {à}*", "*Je pense à toi.*"],
            ["dream **about / of**", "*rêver {de}*", "*Elle rêve de voyager.*"],
            ["trust (someone)", "*faire confiance {à}*", "*Je fais confiance à mes amis.*"],
            ["marry (someone)", "*épouser* (direct) · *se marier {avec}*", "*Il a épousé Claire.*"],
            ["play (an instrument)", "*jouer {de}*", "*Il joue de la guitare.*"],
            ["play (a sport, a game)", "*jouer {à}*", "*Nous jouons au tennis.*"],
            ["call, phone", "*appeler* (direct) · *téléphoner {à}*", "*J'appelle Paul. Je téléphone à Paul.*"],
            ["remember", "*se souvenir {de}* · *se rappeler* (direct)", "*Je me souviens de lui. Je me rappelle ce jour.*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Jouer à or jouer de",
          "text": "If you play it (sport, game): *à*. If it makes music (instrument): *de*. Both merge with the article [[9]]: *jouer {au} foot, jouer {du} piano*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "infinitivo",
      "title": "Verb + de / à + infinitive",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "English uses «to» before most infinitives («decide to go»). French uses **de** with many verbs, **à** with some, and **nothing** with others."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["+ de", "+ à", "Nothing"],
          "rows": [
            ["*décider {de}* (decide to)", "*commencer {à}* (start to)", "*vouloir* (want to)"],
            ["*oublier {de}* (forget to)", "*apprendre {à}* (learn to)", "*pouvoir* (can)"],
            ["*essayer {de}* (try to)", "*aider {à}* (help to)", "*devoir* (must)"],
            ["*arrêter {de}* (stop …ing)", "*réussir {à}* (manage to)", "*aimer, préférer* (like, prefer)"],
            ["*promettre {de}* (promise to)", "*continuer {à}* (keep …ing)", "*aller, savoir*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "J'ai décidé {d'}apprendre le français.", "tr": "I decided to learn French." },
            { "fr": "N'oublie pas {de} fermer la porte.", "tr": "Don't forget to close the door." },
            { "fr": "Il a réussi {à} trouver un travail.", "tr": "He managed to find a job." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "text": "Before a vowel, *de* becomes *d'*: *essayer {d'}ouvrir, arrêter {d'}écrire*."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
